WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.038
Here's the route.

2
00:00:01.038 --> 00:00:04.785
Book 13's loop has five
steps: test, detect drift,

3
00:00:04.785 --> 00:00:08.926
raise a typed task, actuate,
and close with evidence.

4
00:00:08.926 --> 00:00:11.450
The example guide builds
it in seven gates,

5
00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:13.975
and the workbook's
chapters build the code.

6
00:00:13.975 --> 00:00:17.962
Scene one is the drift
run, Gate 3 and Chapter 6.

7
00:00:17.962 --> 00:00:23.387
Scene two turns her drift into a
typed task, Gate 4, Chapters 1 and 4.

8
00:00:23.387 --> 00:00:28.100
Scene three is least privilege,
Gate 1, Chapters 2 and 3.

9
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.837
Scene four finds why her department
keeps drifting, Gate 2, Chapter 8.

10
00:00:32.837 --> 00:00:34.993
Scene five is actuation, Gate 5,

11
00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:38.787
which the kit's first pass
deliberately doesn't build.

12
00:00:38.787 --> 00:00:42.638
Scene six is the re-read,
Gate 6, Chapter 5.

13
00:00:42.638 --> 00:00:46.763
And scene seven is the
evidence, Gate 7, Chapter 7.

14
00:00:46.763 --> 00:00:48.713
Every scene has the same shape.

15
00:00:48.713 --> 00:00:51.814
First, the story beat: what
happens to Erin's record,

16
00:00:51.814 --> 00:00:56.050
with the code that handles it and
the federal requirement behind it.

17
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:59.209
Then a slide called Try it,
with the exact Lab 1 command

18
00:00:59.209 --> 00:01:02.225
from the workbook and the
output it really printed.

19
00:01:02.225 --> 00:01:03.812
Then a one-question check.

20
00:01:03.812 --> 00:01:08.110
Pause the video if you want to answer
it; the answer opens the next slide.
